id: pm-rl-evalplans
title: Enforce predeclared causal evaluation plans at promotion
description: "Declare target populations, correlation units, sample sizes and fixed stopping rules before experiments. Bind plan identity and clustered observations to comparison and generation promotion."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T21:36:09.182Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T13:55:19.967Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Synthetic correlated cohorts cannot masquerade as independent samples; changed plans invalidate comparison identity. Typed SDK and CLI; compact TOON/JSON; typed refusals with remedies; README and example; non-git real public-tracker validation; npm and Bun CI release gates.
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T21:36:11.512Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against the pinned CLI SDK declarations and sibling package sources/docs: core Plan/Decision stores decisions but has no causal experiment-plan enforcement; pm-jev owns model calibration/evaluation; pm-context supplies context. Existing pm-rl-rsipower supplies one powered dataset and is retained separately. This item adds reusable immutable plan/comparison enforcement and cluster-aware promotion, stacked on PR #94; must merge after #94. Dependency pins remain unchanged. Local verification will be targeted tests, typecheck and lint; full npm/Bun release gates run in CI due shared CPU load."
  "2026-10-21T21:49:50.172Z",codex-agent,"Implemented fixed paired plans in core Plan records, immutable result Decisions, provenance-pinned comparison identities, and authoritative promotion enforcement. Plans pin incumbent provenance, populations, member-to-unit assignments, sample sizes, fixed stopping, objective and criterion. Equal-unit aggregation counts correlated cohorts once; one sealed result per plan. Existing unplanned controllers retain legacy semantics without causal-plan claims. Non-git public validation measured 95 observations as one repository unit: candidate 0.7684210526 vs incumbent 0.2315789474; naive episode-count gate would promote, clustered gate refuses. Read-only public source digest is unchanged; evidence is descriptive replay, not deployed causal benefit."
  "2026-10-21T21:51:52.718Z",codex-agent,"Verification: node --test test/evaluation-plan.test.ts test/promotion.test.ts passes 30/30 with zero skipped. New module focused coverage passes 100 percent lines/branches/functions; full four-dimension gate remains for CI. npm run typecheck, npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run duplicates (zero clones), npm run docstring (49 files; 342 declarations) pass. pm test --run --progress ran the linked correlated-cohort regression successfully (1/1). Behavioral revert proof: changing only evaluatePlan to count episode rows fails the correlated-cohort regression; removing only the authoritative enforcement call fails the real promotion regression. Both reverted variants exit 1; exact source bytes restored and 30/30 rerun passes. Local strict health exposes existing extension skew and fence drift in this shared clone, plus advisory stale/provenance findings; no history or merge repair performed. Fresh CI health and npm/Bun release matrices are required before handoff."
  "2026-10-21T21:53:39.245Z",codex-agent,"Packed real-CLI acceptance also passes on the same read-only public snapshot in a non-git scratch tracker, with no Git executable for plan register/show/evaluate. Measured JSON evaluation output is 780 bytes and TOON plan summary is 280 bytes for the 95-item cohort. Source digest remains unchanged. Report and reproducible acceptance runner are linked. No new CLI/SDK defect was found; existing shared-clone health limitations are separate from fresh CI evidence."
  "2026-10-21T21:56:55.154Z",codex-agent,"Final score-contract review added refusals when the held-out score seed_set differs from the frozen comparison hash or its normalization scale differs from the declared reward-bound width. These changes are covered in the real SDK rejection table, and the 30/30 targeted suite, typecheck, test compilation and lint pass again. Packed JSON/TOON public acceptance was renewed with the same 95-observation/one-unit refusal and unchanged source digest. PR #97 is ready for review against main, stacked after #94. Fresh CI tracker health has passed in all three matrix jobs; release gates are still running."
  "2026-10-21T22:01:50.897Z",codex-agent,"Implementation is complete and PR #97 is ready for review, with code commits aec68b7 and 1feca50. Local targeted verification is 30/30 and packed public acceptance is renewed; details are in prior comments and the committed aggregate report. The PR is the live evidence link for final npm Node 22/26 and Bun CI results; all three fresh-checkout health steps have passed and current-head CodeQL has passed. Full release checks are still running and must pass before the final handoff report. The claim is released while those external gates finish; this item intentionally remains in_progress for orchestrator verification. No merge, release, dependency bump, history rewrite or repair was performed. Automated review availability is limited; skipped or quota-limited receipts are not approvals."
  "2026-10-21T22:09:28.591Z",codex-agent,"Final malformed-input review found and fixed one direction coercion edge: a JSON array containing maximize could pass a String-based enum check. The new malformed-direction regression fails with only the prior parser behavior (exit 1), then passes after strict literal validation. The complete focused suite passes 30/30 again; typecheck, test compilation, lint and renewed packed real-CLI public validation pass. The public report numbers and source digest are unchanged. No API design or thresholds changed; final CI is being restarted for this fix."
  "2026-10-22T10:35:55.186Z",codex-agent,"PR #97 review round: pulled the remote head, confirmed main is already an ancestor, and merged the finished PR #94 branch. Review-thread pagination is complete: zero unresolved threads and no published CodeRabbit review body. Verified the requested CodeQL regular-expression issue in the shared generation fence reader; whole-diff review found the same expression in collection-run multi-fence verification. Replace every shared single-fence reader and the multi-fence reader with one forward indexOf scan preserving exact LF/nonempty semantics. Add a subprocess-bounded 100,000-repetition adversarial input and delimiter/first-match regressions. Preserve all release thresholds; verify full npm/Bun gates in CI after local focused checks."
  "2026-10-22T10:38:13.192Z",codex-agent,"CodeQL behavioral revert proof: replaced only jsonSpecFences with the prior regex matching behavior, leaving every new caller and test unchanged. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"generation JSON fence scan bounds\" test/evaluation-plan.test.ts failed 0/1, exit 1, with execFileSync ETIMEDOUT at the 20-second subprocess bound on 100,000 repeated unclosed openers. Restored exact fixed scanner bytes. node --test test/evaluation-plan.test.ts test/promotion.test.ts passes 32/32, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo. The restored adversarial scan itself must finish within two seconds (startup excluded); valid, absent, CRLF, empty and first-match fence cases pass. Entire single-fence and multi-fence reader inventory now uses the same linear iterator. Full PR self-review found no other instance of this regex class. No dist files are tracked."
  "2026-10-22T10:38:44.248Z",codex-agent,"Restored-source validation passes: npm run typecheck, npm run build, npm run build:test, strict ESLint on both changed TypeScript files, npm run duplicates (zero clones), npm run docstring (49 sources, 343 declarations), npm run changelog:full and npm run changelog:check. Pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress passes the two fence regressions (one linked command). Full unchanged npm/Bun release gates and CodeQL will be verified from completed CI logs before starting PR #96. No merge receipts are pending; existing shared-clone extension-version and stale/provenance health advisories remain separately documented."
  "2026-10-22T11:14:00.365Z",codex-agent,"Complete required release gates verified at ae89b6ff0550fcd293ca75f83b91efbace1d837d: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39764672102 . Independently downloaded completed Node 26 npm and Bun job logs: each passes 703/703, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, four coverage dimensions 100/100/100/100 across all 49 authored sources. Strict fresh-checkout health, unscoped lint, zero duplication, 343 declarations, attestation, audit, packaging, changelog, and Bun graph installation pass. CodeQL analysis and security check pass with the polynomial regex removed. Node 22 is still running at this receipt. Local duplicate full gates were stopped after the complete CI npm/Bun passes; they are not counted as full local passes. No thresholds, dependency pins or gate scripts changed. Claim remains released; leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification. No new pm CLI/SDK defect found."
  "2026-10-22T13:32:24.912Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up after PR #94 squash merge: pull the current PR #97 head, merge origin/main, preserve the predeclared evaluation-plan feature and the already verified linear fence scanner, resolve only genuine overlap, regenerate CHANGELOG.md and build outputs, then run unchanged full npm/Bun release gates. Prior focused tests and revert proofs remain valid evidence and will not be repeated unless resolution changes their behavior. Keep histories append-only and leave the item open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-22T13:35:13.419Z",codex-agent,"Merged main 2663828, including the #94 and #96 squash commits. Resolved one index.ts import block by retaining the evaluation-plan import, and four package.json list blocks by retaining main corpus entries plus evaluation-plan package/test/docs/example entries. Both resolved files are byte-identical to the prior reviewed PR #97 versions; all corpus implementation and tests match main. Regenerated CHANGELOG.md via npm run changelog:full and rebuilt ignored dist via npm run build; no dist files are tracked. npm ci and changelog check pass. The diff against main now contains only this feature, its existing linear fence fix, and package-owned evidence. No pending merge receipts were reported. Shared-clone health retains the existing global-extension skew; verify isolated strict health and complete unchanged npm/Bun release gates on the merged candidate in CI."
  "2026-10-22T13:55:17.869Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up complete gates at merged head fbf194f42cbe6c76540fa9b73319e0802de0e2aa: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39788287275 . Downloaded all three completed job logs independently. npm release:check on Node 22, npm release:check on Node 26, and Bun release:check on Node 26 each pass 703/703, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, four 100 percent coverage dimensions across 49 source files. Fresh-checkout strict health, unscoped lint, zero duplication, 343 documented declarations, attestation, audit, package graph installation, packaging and changelog pass; CodeQL passes. Bun CI step metadata remained pending until completion; an isolated Bun 1.3.14/Node 26 local fallback passed static checks and early acceptance cases, then was stopped after CI completed and is not counted as a full local pass. All non-tracker source/tests match the pre-merge reviewed head, so existing revert proofs apply without repeating them. Only the evaluation-plan feature/evidence remains in the diff against main. Regenerated changelog matches main; dist rebuilt and remains ignored. Leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
